{
  "summary": "P1 \u2013 Office-wide internet outage reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, America/New_York). Report: \"The whole office just lost internet. Nobody on the floor can work.\" Checked: account active, no issues. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online with last check-in 2026-10-09T14:41:48Z, no warnings. That may be from before the outage, or it may mean the outage is partial (for example a single floor, Wi-Fi only, or DNS). KB-014 says to escalate when the office network is down for several people. Tier 1 can't diagnose the office network (WAN/ISP link, firewall, core switch, Wi-Fi controllers, DNS/DHCP). Still needed: confirm which site/floor and how widespread it is, check ISP circuit and edge devices, and tell users. Suggest a phone hotspot as a stopgap for urgent work.",
  "reason": "P1 office-wide network outage; KB-014 escalation criterion met and outside Tier 1 tools"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Priya, thanks for reporting this so fast. Since the whole floor has lost internet, I've passed this to our network engineers as a top-priority outage, and they're picking it up now. To help them, please reply with which office and floor this is, roughly when it started, and whether both wired and Wi-Fi connections are down. If anyone needs to get urgent work done in the meantime, they can use a phone hotspot. We'll keep you posted as the engineers find out more.",
  "internal_note": "P1 office-wide internet outage. Sender: Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3). Her account is active with no issues. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online, last check-in 2026-10-09T14:41:48Z, no warnings. That check-in may be from before the outage started, or the outage may be partial (one floor, Wi-Fi only, or DNS). KB-014 says to escalate when the office network is down for several people, and Tier 1 has no tools for network or edge devices. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1). I've asked the user for the site/floor, start time, and whether wired connections are also down.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
